From 85ca1b91c715e99558762f12716843e048c4e37c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:22:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] virtio/gpu(macos): map Venus blobs through
 virglrenderer's shm fds

v1.19.6 on macOS depends on slp's virglrenderer fork (0.10.4e-krunkit):
virgl_renderer_resource_get_map_ptr() and VIRGL_RENDERER_BLOB_FD_TYPE_APPLE,
i.e. a vkMapMemory pointer handed to hv_vm_map. Upstream virglrenderer's
macOS Venus (and UTM's fork of it, which emulates dma_buf/drm modifiers for
the guest) instead backs host-visible and exportable memory with POSIX shm
imported into MoltenVK, and exports it as a VIRGL_RENDERER_BLOB_FD_TYPE_SHM
fd. Drop the map_ptr API from rutabaga and, on macOS, map the shm fd into the
VMM once per resource (whole host pages; a short fd leaves an anonymous zero
tail instead of faulting) and hv_vm_map that. Blobs that are not aligned to
the host page are refused with a clear error: rounding would map over the
guest's next blob, and a guest honoring VIRTIO_GPU_F_BLOB_ALIGNMENT never
sends them. The host mapping is released when the resource is unreferenced.

Upstream virglrenderer runs Venus only behind its render server and libkrun
never polls the renderer, so with VIRGLRENDERER_VENUS on macOS also request
VIRGLRENDERER_RENDER_SERVER and VIRGLRENDERER_USE_ASYNC_FENCE_CB.
